      "message": "I think it would be best to split this up into separate CLs.  I don\u0027t like overloading the meaning of board_get_usb_pd_port_count().\n\n1. Add a function usb_pd_get_port_count().  Replace all callers to board_get_usb_pd_port_count() with usb_pd_get_port_count().\n    uint8_t usb_pd_get_port_count(void)\n    {\n        board_get_usb_pd_port_count();\n    }\n\n2. Add CONFIG_USB_PD_COUNT_RUNTIME and usb_pd_set_port_count()\n    static uint8_t usb_pd_port_count \u003d CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT;\n    uint8_t usb_pd_get_port_count(void)\n    {\n        if (CONFIG_USB_PD_COUNT_RUNTIME)\n            return usb_pd_port_count;\n        else\n            board_get_usb_pd_port_count();\n    }\n    void usb_pd_set_port_count(uint8_t count)\n        usb_pd_port_count \u003d count;\n\n3. Follow on cleanup - remove board_get_usb_pd_port_count(), converting all instances to CONFIG_USB_PD_COUNT_RUNTIME\u003dy and a call to usb_pd_set_port_count() during HOOK_INIT.  This allows for a inline constant when runtime change of the PD port count is not used.\n    #ifndef CONFIG_USB_PD_COUNT_RUNTIME\n    static inline uint8_t usb_pd_get_port_count(void)\n        return CONFIG_USB_PD_COUNT_RUNTIME;\n   \nThere is also board_is_usb_pd_port_present(), which doesn\u0027t appear to have any __override implementations - there is only the default __overridable implementation.",
